; The SUPPORTED-name half of the `.default` head check: `tdate` is a supported prelude name with no
; rust primitive behind it, so a default has nothing to be written into and the shape is refused —
; with no name refusal anywhere in the run to piggyback on. This is what pins the check at the
; `.default` APPLICATION rather than at a name seam: the sibling fixture
; (`tests/robustness/ctl_default_unmapped_head.cddl`) would still refuse if the check lived at the
; refused-name seam, and this one would not.
x = tdate .default 1
